{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.LatticeGaugeShadow","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.LatticeGaugeShadow","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Trace","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.LatticeGaugeShadow.matrix_trace_annihilates_orderingDefect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.LatticeGaugeShadow.matrix_trace_annihilates_orderingDefect","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/LatticeGaugeShadow.lean#L128-L138","doc":"**Concrete realisation via the matrix trace.** The genuine block-trace\ncharacter `Matrix.trace` (a class function on the Hecke block's\nrepresentation) annihilates the ordering defect: `tr(A·B − B·A) = 0`.\nUses `Matrix.trace_mul_comm` (`tr(A·B) = tr(B·A)`) — the concrete\ncyclicity. This is the σ₁³-agent's `tr[A,B] = 0 @ 40 dps` as an exact\ntheorem. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.LatticeGaugeShadow.CyclicCharacter.annihilates_surfaceOrderingCorrection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.LatticeGaugeShadow.CyclicCharacter.annihilates_surfaceOrderingCorrection","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/LatticeGaugeShadow.lean#L114-L126","doc":"**Null scalar channel (full surface correction).** A surface-ordering\ncorrection is a sum, over the plaquettes/cells of the tessellation, of\nordering defects `∑ᵢ (Aᵢ·Bᵢ − Bᵢ·Aᵢ)`. The block-trace character\nannihilates the whole sum: the scalar channel of the surface state-sum's\nordering correction is null. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.LatticeGaugeShadow.CyclicCharacter.annihilates_orderingDefect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.LatticeGaugeShadow.CyclicCharacter.annihilates_orderingDefect","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/LatticeGaugeShadow.lean#L105-L112","doc":"**Null scalar channel (single cell pair).** A block-trace character\nannihilates the surface-ordering defect: `χ(A·B − B·A) = 0`. The scalar\n(character) channel of the surface-ordering correction vanishes — the\nrigorous version of the numerical `tr[A,B] = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.LatticeGaugeShadow.CyclicCharacter.cyclic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.LatticeGaugeShadow.CyclicCharacter.cyclic","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/LatticeGaugeShadow.lean#L103-L103","doc":"**Cyclicity** — the defining property of a trace / class function:\n`χ(a·b) = χ(b·a)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.LatticeGaugeShadow.CyclicCharacter.toHom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.LatticeGaugeShadow.CyclicCharacter.toHom","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/LatticeGaugeShadow.lean#L100-L100","doc":"The underlying additive functional (a class function is additive). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.LatticeGaugeShadow.CyclicCharacter.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.LatticeGaugeShadow.CyclicCharacter.mk","kind":"ctor","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/LatticeGaugeShadow.lean#L98-L98","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.LatticeGaugeShadow.CyclicCharacter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.LatticeGaugeShadow.CyclicCharacter","kind":"structure","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/LatticeGaugeShadow.lean#L92-L103","doc":"A **block-trace character** `χ^λ`: a cyclic additive functional on the\nholonomy ring. The two fields are the genuine defining properties of a\nclass function / trace: additivity (`toHom : R →+ S`) and cyclicity\n(`χ(a·b) = χ(b·a)`). The concrete matrix trace `Matrix.trace` is such a\ncharacter (see `matrix_trace_annihilates_orderingDefect`), so the notion\nis inhabited by a real object, not a stub. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.LatticeGaugeShadow.orderingDefect_antisymm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.LatticeGaugeShadow.orderingDefect_antisymm","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/LatticeGaugeShadow.lean#L85-L90","doc":"The ordering defect is antisymmetric in the two cells:\n`orderingDefect B A = − orderingDefect A B`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.LatticeGaugeShadow.orderingDefect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.LatticeGaugeShadow.orderingDefect","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/LatticeGaugeShadow.lean#L77-L83","doc":"The **surface-ordering defect** (additive commutator) of two cell\nholonomies `A, B`. This is exactly the `q`-curvature transport defect\n`F_q = (1 + δq₁)(1 + δq₂) − (1 + δq₂)(1 + δq₁)` of\n`QOU.LocalQ.ObservationParallelogram.Fq` specialised to the two cell\nholonomies (both are `A·B − B·A`), and the obstruction to two adjacent\ncells commuting. ","signatureChunk":0}]}